<Layout
  title="Terafab — Hardware — Rycode"
  description="Planned semiconductor fab (SpaceX + Tesla). Not a training data center."
  variant="ai"
>
  <article class="ai-model">
    <p class="ai-model-kicker">Hardware · Chip fab</p>
    <h1 class="ai-model-title">Terafab</h1>
    <p class="ai-model-dek">A planned semiconductor fabrication plant. Spelling: Terafab (one word). It is not Colossus, not Memphis, and not a training campus. Fab makes chips. Campus trains models.</p>
    <hr class="ai-model-rule" />

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">What it is</h2>
    <p>Company text (SpaceX Updates Terafab; terafab.ai): a vertically integrated advanced semiconductor fab — logic + memory + advanced packaging (+ testing) under one roof. Joint SpaceX + Tesla effort for the initial phase. xAI / SpaceXAI sits in the compute-demand story (chips for space-based data centers), not named as co-investor in the Aug 2026 SpaceX site announcement.</p>
    <p>Stated purpose: close the gap between global chip supply and future compute demand; chips for Tesla Optimus / Cybercab-class edge inference <strong>and</strong> high-power chips for SpaceX space-based data centers.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Where</h2>
    <p><strong>Full-scale site:</strong> Grimes County, Texas (near College Station / Houston). <strong>Precursor:</strong> Tesla research fab broken ground Apr 2026 on the North Campus of Giga Texas (Austin). Both from SpaceX Updates / SpaceX sites.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Capex — keep the labels</h2>
    <p>Do not mix these as one “cost of Terafab.”</p>
    <div class="ai-model-table-wrap">
      <table class="ai-model-table ai-model-table--prose">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Figure</th>
            <th scope="col">Label</th>
            <th scope="col">Source</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Phase 1 ~$16.8B; &gt;100 million sq ft planned; ≥3,000 jobs</td>
            <td>Public (company) — Aug 2026 announcement</td>
            <td><a href="https://www.spacex.com/updates/terafab">SpaceX Updates Terafab</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Phase ~$55B; full buildout up to ~$119B</td>
            <td>Earlier filing / county-notice reporting — supersession risk</td>
            <td>CNBC / The Register summarizing May 2026 Grimes County public-hearing notice</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>“1 terawatt of compute per year”</td>
            <td>Company marketing / founder ambition — not a built facility metric</td>
            <td><a href="https://terafab.ai/">terafab.ai</a></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>TW/year is a chip-output ambition. It is not a site electrical load. Do not put it next to Colossus MW as if they shared a unit.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Do not claim</h2>
    <p>Terafab is not operational at Grimes. It is not the Memphis data center. Process node, wafer starts, yield, and first-production date are not on the SpaceX Terafab page as of the 13 Sep 2026 pack — open. Intel as co-developer / 14A node appears in secondary press, not in the Aug 2026 SpaceX Terafab announcement text: label unconfirmed / dropped from later company text until a primary confirms.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Peer (fab, not campus)</h2>
    <p>TSMC Arizona (company): investment path $12B → $265B planned; 10 fabs, 2 advanced packaging, R&amp;D; campus &gt;1,100 acres; Fab1 N4 HVM since Q4 2024. That is a proven US leading-edge foundry buildout. Different ownership model (merchant foundry vs SpaceX + Tesla captive claim).</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="ai-model-sources">
      <li><a href="https://www.spacex.com/updates/terafab">SpaceX Updates — Terafab</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.spacex.com/sites">SpaceX sites</a> (Grimes County)</li>
      <li><a href="https://terafab.ai/">terafab.ai</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.tsmc.com/static/abouttsmcaz/index.htm">TSMC Arizona</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.cnbc.com/2026/05/06/elon-musks-spacex-chip-fab-in-texas-to-cost-up-to-119-billion.html">CNBC, 6 May 2026</a> — earlier filing figures</li>
      <li><a href="/ai/hardware/memphis-colossus/">Memphis / Colossus</a> — the campus, not this plant</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Layout>
